{"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The shortest tour, by Held–Karp dynamic programming (Bellman, “Dynamic programming"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"treatment of the travelling salesman problem”, Journal of the ACM 9, 1962; Held and Karp,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"“A dynamic programming approach to sequencing problems”, Journal of SIAM 10, 1962): the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"least-weight Hamiltonian cycle of the simple graph, or nil when there is none; among the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optimal ones, the lexicographically least by vertex number listed from the first vertex"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"(JGraphT "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"HeldKarpTSP"},{"type":"text","text":"’s tour). The graph need not be complete: a missing pair is an absent"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"edge. Tours read the simple graph, as "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nearestNeighborTour(weight:)"},{"type":"text","text":" documents; nil below"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"three vertices."}],"kind":"symbol","metadata":{"title":"shortestTour(weight:)","roleHeading":"Instance Method","extendedModule":"GraphProtocols","modules":[{"relatedModules":["GraphProtocols"],"name":"Tours"}],"symbolKind":"method","externalID":"s:14GraphProtocols0A0P5ToursE12shortestTour6weight5Walks5CycleVy6VertexQz5Edges_5IndexQZGSgqd__ANXE_ts18AdditiveArithmeticRd__SLRd__lF","remoteSource":{"url":"https:\/\/github.com\/Tyler-Keith-Thompson\/Grafluent\/blob\/main\/Sources\/Tours\/HeldKarp.swift#L186","fileName":"HeldKarp.swift"},"fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"shortestTour","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"W","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":">(","kind":"text"},{"text":"weight","kind":"externalParam"},{"text":": (","kind":"text"},{"text":"Self","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"."